{"chunk_id": "63cdace178d8", "text": "Sage Vasishtha urges Rama to accept the throne of Ayodhya, arguing from tradition, duty, and the authority of elders. He reminds Rama that in the Ikshvaku dynasty the eldest son must rule and that obedience to parents, mother, father, and spiritual teacher forms the foundation of righteousness. Rama replies respectfully but remains firm: the debt owed to one\u2019s parents is immeasurable, and his father Dasaratha\u2019s command must not be broken. Hearing this, Bharata is overcome with grief and adopts a desperate vow, seating himself on kusa grass before Rama\u2019s hut and declaring he will fast and lie at the doorway like a supplicant until Rama agrees to return. Rama gently rebukes him, saying such behavior is unfit for a king, but Bharata persists, and the assembled people admit they cannot sway Rama from obeying his father\u2019s command.\nVasishtha urges Rama to accept the throne, but Rama insists on obeying Dasharatha\u2019s command as Bharata mournfully pleads for his return.\nThemes: filial obedience, dharma and duty, royal succession, brotherly devotion, guru counsel", "vector": [0.016546662896871567, -0.021039821207523346, -0.029730182141065598, -0.0007911793072707951, -0.016291063278913498, 0.019169913604855537, -0.020636243745684624, -0.012645416893064976, -0.02039409801363945, -0.01049973163753748, 0.021833522245287895, -0.01462294440716505, 0.003474126337096095, 0.017569057643413544, -0.013116256333887577, 0.004086218308657408, 0.04977451264858246, -0.012241839431226254, 0.036913853138685226, 0.005034624598920345, 0.002022930420935154, -0.011818083003163338, 0.0025475805159658194, 0.007203851826488972, -0.022963538765907288, 0.007708323188126087, 0.01380233746021986, -0.02081112749874592, 0.007028968073427677, -0.017999539151787758, -0.010708246380090714, -0.015093784779310226, 0.006463960278779268, -0.008670181967318058, -0.029138268902897835, 7.299070421140641e-05, -0.01471711229532957, -0.021107083186507225, 